## 6. Installation and Setup

### Prerequisites

- Python 3.10–3.14, subject to dependency compatibility
- pip package manager
- Git (optional, for repository management)
- A modern web browser

### Step 1: Clone the repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/harshitshukla7220/cognevance_AI-Chatbot-NLP.git
cd cognevance_AI-Chatbot-NLP
```

### Step 2: Create a virtual environment

On Windows:

```powershell
py -m venv .venv
.\.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
```

If PowerShell blocks script activation, use:

```powershell
Set-ExecutionPolicy -Scope Process -ExecutionPolicy RemoteSigned
.\.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
```

### Step 3: Install dependencies

```bash
python -m pip install --upgrade pip
python -m pip install -r requirements.txt
```

### Step 4: Train the model

```bash
python train.py
```

This trains the intent-classification model using the training dataset and saves the resulting model in the `models/` directory.

### Step 5: Run the application

```bash
python app.py
```

Open the following URL in your browser:

http://127.0.0.1:5000

Keep the terminal running while using the chatbot.

## 7. Testing

Run the unit tests using:

```bash
python -m unittest discover -s tests -v
```

Run the evaluation script using:

```bash
python evaluate.py
```

The tests cover intent classification, preprocessing, fallback behavior, knowledge-base retrieval, model persistence, dataset integrity, and Flask endpoints.

## 8. Model Evaluation

The recorded evaluation report contains the following results:

| Evaluation Metric | Baseline | Improved Pipeline |
|---|---:|---:|
| Five-fold cross-validation accuracy | 65.5% | 77.2% |
| Held-out test accuracy | 83.1% | 98.5% |
| Held-out macro F1-score | 0.836 | 0.984 |

The improved pipeline combines NLTK-based stemming with word-level and character-level TF-IDF features.

**Evaluation note:** The held-out result may be optimistic because the dataset was refined after reviewing misclassified examples. Cross-validation provides a more conservative estimate of performance. These results should not be interpreted as a guarantee of accuracy on unseen real-world conversations.

